WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.249 --> 00:00:07.954
India is one of the oldest countries in the world.

2
00:00:08.635 --> 00:00:11.597
This fascinating place has a diverse and colorful history.

3
00:00:12.418 --> 00:00:18.503
Almost one-fifth of the entire world's population lives in India; it is the second most populous country on

4
00:00:18.603 --> 00:00:19.964
earth, after China!

5
00:00:22.546 --> 00:00:25.329
Its geography is as diverse as its people.

6
00:00:25.929 --> 00:00:31.009
It has high mountains in the north, dry deserts in the west, and tropical beaches in the south.

7
00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:36.771
The people of India have adapted to life in all these different climates, and this is reflected in

8
00:00:36.791 --> 00:00:39.032
their culture, heritage, and language.

9
00:00:42.454 --> 00:00:44.415
The people of India love to celebrate life.

10
00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:50.177
They are proud of their rich traditions and vibrant culture, and love to gather to celebrate any occasion.

11
00:00:51.118 --> 00:00:52.978
This is why they have many different festivals.

12
00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:56.400
There are hundreds of festivals all across India every month.

13
00:00:57.036 --> 00:01:00.077
There are so many that there is a holiday for every day of the year.

14
00:01:03.178 --> 00:01:07.919
Some festivals last only a day, some one week, and some last a whole month!

15
00:01:08.679 --> 00:01:14.321
Most often, Indian people celebrate the changing of the seasons, the beginning of the harvest, the full moon,

16
00:01:14.821 --> 00:01:16.021
and the arrival of rain.

17
00:01:16.921 --> 00:01:23.463
They also honor religious and national holidays such as the birthdays of saints, national heroes, and gurus.

18
00:01:24.344 --> 00:01:27.785
Each festival has a different name and is celebrated in a different way.

19
00:01:29.785 --> 00:01:36.247
Holi, the Festival of Colors One of the most popular festivals in India is the festival of Holi.

20
00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:40.628
This festival marks the end of winter and the beginning of the first harvest.

21
00:01:41.828 --> 00:01:45.349
It is usually celebrated at the end of February or the beginning of March.

22
00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:48.410
It starts on the night of the first full moon of spring.

23
00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:53.652
People begin to celebrate by lighting large bonfires in the middle of their towns to scare away evil

24
00:01:53.692 --> 00:01:54.572
spirits and ghosts.

25
00:01:58.272 --> 00:02:03.716
The following morning they run around the streets spraying each other with brightly colored powders and colored water.

26
00:02:04.797 --> 00:02:07.598
This is a time when people forget their worries and have fun.

27
00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:11.001
Everyone gets completely covered in a rainbow of colors.

28
00:02:11.721 --> 00:02:16.204
Around lunchtime the celebrations end, and people head to the river to wash off.

29
00:02:16.905 --> 00:02:19.286
They spend the rest of the day at home with their families.

30
00:02:21.288 --> 00:02:27.452
Diwali, the Festival of Lights Another popular festival is Diwali, or the festival of lights.

31
00:02:28.208 --> 00:02:33.090
All people─rich and poor, old and young, men and women─celebrate it.

32
00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:40.053
It is a four-day-long celebration, during which people decorate their homes with lanterns and set beautiful candles adrift

33
00:02:40.113 --> 00:02:41.334
on rivers or the ocean.

34
00:02:44.615 --> 00:02:50.197
By lighting lanterns, people thank their gods for giving them health, happiness, children, and knowledge.

35
00:02:50.978 --> 00:02:56.000
Diwali gives people a chance to scare away dark spirits and welcome light into their lives.

36
00:02:56.968 --> 00:03:00.009
The festival ends with a beautiful fireworks display at night.

37
00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:10.714
Makar Sankranti, the Festival of Kites A festival called Makar Sankranti celebrates the end of the long winter

38
00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:14.755
when the sun enters the northern hemisphere, which occurs on January 14.

39
00:03:15.616 --> 00:03:20.898
The sky fills up with hundreds of colorful shapes as people gather to fly kites, each one more

40
00:03:20.958 --> 00:03:22.018
beautiful than the next.

41
00:03:23.279 --> 00:03:28.541
People receive prizes for the most original kite or for flying their kite with the most skill.

42
00:03:29.322 --> 00:03:34.525
At night, people light lanterns, attach them to their kites, and fill the night sky with thousands of

43
00:03:34.565 --> 00:03:35.325
glowing lights.

44
00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:43.850
Gandhi Festival Each year on October 2, the people of India gather to celebrate the birth of their

45
00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.871
national hero, Mahatma Gandhi.

46
00:03:46.952 --> 00:03:49.873
Gandhi fought to free India from British rule without violence.

47
00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:54.256
He led peaceful marches throughout the country and united the people of India.

48
00:03:55.100 --> 00:04:01.122
On this national holiday, people visit the many statues of Gandhi all around India and sing Gandhi's favorite

49
00:04:01.162 --> 00:04:09.304
songs. Yugadi, the Hindu New Year Yugadi is the New Year celebration in the Hindu calendar.

50
00:04:10.104 --> 00:04:12.845
Each year it falls on a different day between March and April.

51
00:04:13.565 --> 00:04:15.586
It is a day of forgiveness and new beginnings.

52
00:04:16.326 --> 00:04:20.607
On the day of the holiday, people exchange sweets and ask each other for forgiveness.

53
00:04:21.607 --> 00:04:25.120
It is a day when merchants and accountants pay their debts as well.

54
00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:34.263
Dasara, the Festival of Good and Evil Dasara is a ten-day festival that celebrates the victory of good

55
00:04:34.443 --> 00:04:35.003
over evil.

56
00:04:35.703 --> 00:04:38.244
It is held in the town of Mysore in October.

57
00:04:39.124 --> 00:04:41.745
The whole town celebrates with concerts and dances.

58
00:04:42.665 --> 00:04:46.706
People decorate their homes with lanterns, candles, and flowers for nine days.

59
00:04:47.347 --> 00:04:52.148
On the tenth day, everyone dresses up in a colorful costumes and dances all around the town.

60
00:04:54.920 --> 00:05:01.203
This carnival is a rich celebration full of musicians, clowns, decorated elephants, and traditional dancers.

61
00:05:02.383 --> 00:05:06.985
The people of India are proud of their country's heritage, and this pride shows in the way they

62
00:05:07.025 --> 00:05:07.786
celebrate life.

63
00:05:08.386 --> 00:05:14.589
By honoring their traditions with colorful festivals, they show their respect and appreciation for India's rich and varied

64
00:05:14.629 --> 00:05:20.752
culture. Every day is a festival of a different kind, making India a very exciting place!
